:**AC-5.1:** The user can detach a source attachment from current project or\n512:**AC-5.2:** Detaching a source attachment does not erase prior visible\n520:**AC-5.3:** Detaching one source attachment does not remove unrelated current\n528:### 6. Returning Later and Handling Unavailable or Degraded Source State\n544:**AC-6.1:** Reloading or reopening the project shell or process work surface\n556:**AC-6.2:** If a requested source attachment is unavailable or access is\n569:**AC-6.3:** If one source attachment fails independently, the rest of the\n579:## Data Contracts\n581:### Browser Routes\n593:### Endpoints\n606:### Source Attachment Request\n626:### Source Attachment Update Request\n634:### Source Attachment Summary\n658:### Source Provenance Entry\n675:### Attach Source Attachment Response\n681:### Update Source Attachment Response\n687:### Refresh Source Attachment Response\n695:### Detach Source Attachment Response\n703:### Source Provenance Response\n715:### Refresh Failure Boundary\n728:### Error Responses\n744:## Dependencies\n767:## Non-Functional Requirements\n769:### Performance\n779:### Security\n787:### Reliability\n800:### Accessibility\n807:### Observability\n816:## Tech Design Questions\n849:## Recommended Story Breakdown\n855:### Story 0: Foundation (Infrastructure)\n862:### Story 1: Attach Repositories to a Project or Process\n873:### Story 2: Manage Purpose, Access Mode, and Target Ref\n885:### Story 3: Hydration and Freshness Management\n897:### Story 4: Provenance and Canonical Source Visibility\n910:### Story 5: Detach Sources and Preserve Prior Provenance\n921:### Story 6: Reopen and Degraded Source State\n934:## Validation Checklist\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
