{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_89","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"outcome\":\"block\",\"crossStoryFindings\":[\"Current-source semantics are split across the epic: process materials, checkpointing, and rebuild planning use `resolveActiveProcessSourceAttachments`, but refresh targeting, project-shell refresh eligibility, and informed-work provenance still trust raw durable `currentMaterialRefs.sourceAttachmentIds`.\",\"Soft detach and process-scope shadowing therefore stop at the read-model boundary; some runtime paths still treat detached or shadowed rows as current after the UI has hidden or replaced them.\",\"The provenance API shape is ahead of the runtime: degraded visibility modes such as `redacted` exist in the contract and renderer, but not in any real production write path.\"],\"architectureFindings\":[\"The tech design makes active-source resolution the canonical rule for combining project-scoped and process-scoped sources, but `RuntimeSourceHydrationExecutor` and `DefaultSourceProvenanceService.recordInformedWorkForCurrentSources` bypass that policy and reconstruct their own source sets from raw refs.\",\"Soft detach is implemented durably (`detachedAt`, `detachedByUserId`) and respected by the main readers, but older raw-ref consumers can still pull detached rows back into refresh/recovery decisions.\",\"The published provenance contract advertises `currentAttachmentVisibility: redacted`, but the implementation has no architecture path that detects revoked enrichment access and materializes that state.\"],\"epicCoverageAssessment\":[\"Epic gate passed: `corepack pnpm run verify-all` completed successfully on May 4, 2026. The `test:e2e` leg is still scaffold-only and prints `SKIP: test:e2e scaffolded in Story 0; no executable suite yet`.\",\"Automated coverage exercises attach/update/detach flows, branch-drift freshness, refresh settled/pending/failed responses, and ready/degraded provenance rendering.\",\"Coverage does not exercise shadowed-source refresh/recovery or informed-work provenance recording when both project- and process-scoped ids remain durably current; the only explicit shadowing check I found is contract/fixture-level (`tests/service/server/source-management-contracts.test.ts:41-62`), and the redacted provenance path is only test-seeded (`tests/service/server/source-management-api.test.ts:1099-1167`).\"],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"Source refresh is wired to real GitHub/provider seams, but its working-set planner still rehydrates from raw durable source ids, so detached or shadowed rows can flow back into a real provider hydration.\",\"The `redacted` provenance visibility branch is currently contract-only: no production writer emits `access_revoked` or any other degraded provenance row for that path.\",\"Process execution still uses the shared Epic 3 placeholder script payload, so the provenance hooks run against a non-domain-specific execution path even though persistence and checkpoint integrations are real.\"],\"blockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EV-06-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Refresh planning bypasses active-source resolution and can rehydrate detached or shadowed-out sources\",\"evidence\":\"`RuntimeSourceHydrationExecutor.refreshRecoverableSource()` resolves target ownership and builds the hydration plan from raw `currentMaterialRefs.sourceAttachmentIds` (`apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-refresh.service.ts:92-159,215-240`) instead of the active-source resolver used by checkpointing and rebuild planning (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/active-process-sources.ts:13-62`, `apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts:751-760,1269-1289`). Because process-scoped attach only appends the new id and detach only stamps `detachedAt` (`convex/sourceAttachments.ts:148-158,279-317`), refreshing one source can still target or hydrate rows that the canonical current-source model has already shadowed or detached. The same raw ids also drive `projectRefreshTargetCount` in the project shell (`apps/platform/server/services/projects/readers/source-section.reader.ts:36-66`).\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-refresh.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/active-process-sources.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/projects/readers/source-section.reader.ts\",\"convex/sourceAttachments.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.3\",\"AC-3.3\",\"AC-5.1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"EV-06-002\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Informed-work provenance ignores shadowing and can record duplicate or wrong-scope source relationships\",\"evidence\":\"`recordInformedWorkForCurrentSources()` iterates `currentMaterialRefs.sourceAttachmentIds` directly and records every distinct id (`apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-provenance.service.ts:36-75`). When a process-scoped attachment shadows a project-scoped sibling, both ids remain durably current because process attach only appends the new id (`convex/sourceAttachments.ts:148-158`), while the canonical current-source read model collapses them via `resolveActiveProcessSourceAttachments()` (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/active-process-sources.ts:13-62`). `buildSourceProvenanceEntry()` then exposes whichever recorded row was stored, including its scope/access/hydration (`apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-provenance.service.ts:174-230`), so provenance can claim both attachments informed the run or attribute informed work to the shadowed project-scoped row that the process materials view no longer shows.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-provenance.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/active-process-sources.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts\",\"convex/sourceAttachments.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.3\",\"AC-4.1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"EV-06-003\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"The shipped runtime cannot produce the required redacted provenance state\",\"evidence\":\"The response contract and renderer support `currentAttachmentVisibility: 'redacted'` / `degradationReason: 'access_revoked'` (`apps/platform/shared/contracts/source-management.ts:97-152`, `apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-provenance.service.ts:202-228`), but the only production write path always persists provenance as `entryStatus: 'ready'` with `degradationReason: null` (`apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-provenance.service.ts:153-171`). The only exercised redacted path is test-seeded data (`tests/service/server/source-management-api.test.ts:1099-1167`). No non-test code writes `access_revoked` or any other degraded provenance row.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-provenance.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/shared/contracts/source-management.ts\",\"apps/platform/shared/contracts/schemas.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-4.4\",\"AC-6.2\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true}],\"nonBlockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EV-06-004\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"Source provenance is wired to the shared placeholder execution payload\",\"evidence\":\"Process execution still defaults to `buildDefaultScriptPayload()` and its embedded placeholder script (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/script-execution.service.ts:9-104`). The epic's real provenance hooks run off that execution/checkpoint path (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts:549-568,830-839`), so informed-work and code-update provenance are currently attached to placeholder execution behavior until process-type-specific orchestration lands.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/script-execution.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/process-environment.service.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":false}],\"unresolvedItems\":[\"AGENTS.md requires `docs/onboarding/current-state-index.md` and related onboarding docs, but `docs/onboarding/` is absent from this checkout, so I had to review directly from the epic spec pack and code.\",\"The fix shape for provenance `access_revoked` is still unsettled: the codebase needs either a real write-time producer or a read-time derivation rule for redacted entries.\",\"There is still no browser-level executable e2e proof for the full attach -> refresh -> provenance journey because `test:e2e` is scaffold-only.\"],\"gateResult\":\"pass\"}"}}
